Changes
-------

The copy differs from the original packages in the ways below. The history
of the repository holds each change with its diff.

- The import paths `marker.`, `surya.`, and `pdftext.` are rewritten to
  `raw2md_engine.marker.`, `raw2md_engine.surya.`, and
  `raw2md_engine.pdftext.`.
- The parts that raw2md does not call are removed: the LLM pass, the
  extraction converter, the config parser, the input formats other than
  PDF, the output formats other than Markdown, and the command-line and
  browser applications.
- The PDF converter builds its provider and its Markdown renderer
  directly.
- The settings are fixed values. They do not load from environment
  variables or from a `local.env` file.
- The copy downloads nothing: no font when the converter starts and no
  model weights. `marker/models.py` takes the folder of the weights from
  its caller.
- The models build their non-persistent buffers on the CPU, and the
  loaders build them again after the load of the weights, before the move
  to the device (2026-10-19). Changed files, under
  src/raw2md_engine/surya/: `common/load.py`, `common/adetr/decoder.py`,
  `common/surya/decoder/__init__.py`, `common/surya/encoder/__init__.py`,
  `ocr_error/model/encoder.py`, `foundation/loader.py`,
  `table_rec/loader.py`, and `ocr_error/loader.py`.
- The copy follows the API of transformers 5 (2026-10-19): the tied
  weights as a mapping, `post_init` in every model, the default rotary
  frequencies and the head mask in the copy itself, the tokenizer helpers
  from their new module, and no head pruning or ONNX configuration.
  Changed files, under src/raw2md_engine/surya/: `common/pretrained.py`,
  `common/adetr/decoder.py`, `common/donut/encoder.py`,
  `common/surya/__init__.py`, `common/surya/decoder/__init__.py`,
  `common/surya/decoder/config.py`, `ocr_error/model/config.py`,
  `ocr_error/model/encoder.py`, `ocr_error/tokenizer.py`,
  `table_rec/model/encoder.py`, and `table_rec/model/encoderdecoder.py`.
- `marker/settings.py` imports torch only when the device is read, so the
  renderers and the text processors import without torch (2026-10-24).
- `marker/renderers/__init__.py` keeps the trailing minus when two inline
  math spans merge (2026-10-24).
- `marker/schema/text/line.py` removes only a hyphen or a soft hyphen at
  the end of a line, and keeps a dash (2026-10-24).
- `marker/renderers/markdown.py` escapes a vertical bar in a table cell
  and does not replace it with a space (2026-10-24).
- `marker/processors/table.py` removes dot leaders in a table cell only
  when whitespace or the end follows them (2026-10-24).
- `marker/schema/text/span.py` applies every format of a span, with math
  innermost and bold outermost (2026-10-24).
- `marker/processors/sectionheader.py` sorts the heading heights together
  with their cluster labels (2026-10-24).
- `marker/schema/text/span.py` does not wrap the text of a math span in
  superscript markup (2026-10-24).
- `pdftext/pdf/pages.py` does not compare a span with the blank spans of
  its line when it decides a superscript or a subscript (2026-10-24).
- `marker/renderers/markdown.py` keeps the escaped space at the end of a
  math span, so a trailing backslash does not escape the closing
  delimiter (2026-10-24).
- `marker/renderers/markdown.py` writes one separator line for a table
  of one row (2026-10-24).

Each changed file of `pdftext/` carries a notice at its top.

Last change: 2026-10-24.
